Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_DRIVER_CACHE_EXIT_ONLY=1: the driver pipeline cache is written at boot and at exit, not during play; off by default

The driver's pipeline cache is written whole every 128 new pipelines, at most every 30 s (or one
second per MiB of cache): vkGetPipelineCacheData into one buffer, then a file beside it, then a
rename. For Ocarina with ~8,700 pipelines the file is 123 MiB (vulkan_pipelines.bin). On a base PS5
near its memory limit that write took 24-55 s, and while it ran everything touching guest memory
stalled: frames of ~960 ms in clusters, one every ~2 s, the guest cores more idle than in smooth
play, single GPU-front reads of guest memory taking 400-920 ms.

waveydude, Jabu-Jabu's Belly, base PS5 13.60:
| Run  | Slow stretch | Write began (from its length) | Write ended (its log line) |
| W-11 | ~211-264 s   | ~206 s (55.4 s)               | 261.3 s                    |
| W-11 | ~419-462 s   | ~415 s (42.1 s)               | 456.8 s                    |
| W-10 | ~423-460 s   | ~433 s (23.9 s)               | ~457 s                     |
(pipeline_cache_save in EDEN_PERF_COST, the 5 s report the stretch ends in.)

With the switch, QueueVulkanPipelineCacheFlush counts the pipeline (the exit write's
EDEN_PE_PIPELINE_CACHE_EXIT check still sees it) and returns. The writes at boot
(LoadDiskResources) and at the end of the session (~PipelineCache) are as before. A crash loses the
driver builds made since boot: those pipelines take their driver compile again next session.
Translations (vulkan.bin) are not this file and are kept as before. One log line at the first new
pipeline. The switch is in the shader-store stamp's list and in its list of switches that never
change a translation (0926), so setting it does not start an empty store.

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
index b64bf28..dace56e 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
@@ -2253,6 +2253,25 @@ void PipelineCache::QueueVulkanPipelineCacheFlush() {
         return;
     }
     pipelines_counted.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_acq_rel);
+    // EDEN_UP_DRIVER_CACHE_EXIT_ONLY=1: the driver's pipeline cache is written when the session
+    // ends (~PipelineCache) and at boot (LoadDiskResources), never during play. Each write copies
+    // the whole cache: 123 MiB for Ocarina with ~8,700 pipelines (vulkan_pipelines.bin). On a base
+    // PS5 near its memory limit that copy took 24-55 s, and the whole time everything touching
+    // guest memory stalled: frames of ~960 ms in clusters, one every ~2 s, in Jabu-Jabu's Belly
+    // (W-10 and W-11; the write's end lines up with each stretch's end: 261.3 s and 456.8 s).
+    // A crash loses the driver builds made since the boot's write (those pipelines take their
+    // driver compile again next time); translations (vulkan.bin) are kept as before.
+    static const bool exit_only = [] {
+        const bool on = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_DRIVER_CACHE_EXIT_ONLY");
+        if (on) {
+            LOG_INFO(Render_Vulkan, "EDEN_UP_DRIVER_CACHE_EXIT_ONLY=1: the driver pipeline cache is "
+                                    "written at boot and when the session ends, not during play");
+        }
+        return on;
+    }();
+    if (exit_only) {
+        return;
+    }
     if (++pipelines_since_flush < VULKAN_CACHE_FLUSH_PIPELINES) {
         return;
     }
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_prep.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_prep.cpp
index 28c2eef..b872fa4 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_prep.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_prep.cpp
@@ -135,6 +135,7 @@ constexpr const char* TranslationSwitches[] = {
     "EDEN_UP_BIND_ON_BACK", "EDEN_UP_BLIT_EDGE_CLAMP", "EDEN_UP_BUFFER_USE_MARKS",
     "EDEN_UP_COMPUTE_INDIRECT_ORDER", "EDEN_UP_DEFERRED_CLEAR_PASS", "EDEN_UP_DJ_CHANNEL_IDS",
     "EDEN_UP_DJ_FRAG_BARRIER", "EDEN_UP_DJ_GATHER_OWNERS", "EDEN_UP_DRAIN_SKIP_SAME",
+    "EDEN_UP_DRIVER_CACHE_EXIT_ONLY",
     "EDEN_UP_EVICT_KEEP_SSBO",
     "EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW", "EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW_OOT_EXEMPT", "EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW_VERIFY",
     "EDEN_UP_FAST_POLL", "EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_BLITSTATE", "EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_CHURN",
@@ -744,6 +745,7 @@ std::string MakeStamp(u32 cache_version, u32 driver_id, u32 driver_version) {
         static constexpr std::string_view NotTranslation[]{
             "EDEN_NX2_TRANSCODE_WAIT",        // a refused ASTC decode waits for its image's next use
             "EDEN_NX2_PRELOAD_ALL_PIPELINES", // which kept pipelines the boot builds
+            "EDEN_UP_DRIVER_CACHE_EXIT_ONLY", // when the driver cache file is written
         };
         if (std::ranges::find(NotTranslation, std::string_view{name}) != std::end(NotTranslation)) {
             continue;
